  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Livelihood Recovery in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon is grappling with economic and financial decline, COVID-19, the disastrous impact of the Beirut Port explosions and continued impact of the Syrian crisis. In addition, political deadlock fuels popular protests and hampers meaningful reform and recovery efforts. Recent hostilities between Israel and Hezbollah has resulted in over 60,000 people becoming internally displaced and exacerbated the strain on livelihoods in the south. In this context, the situation of ordinary people in Lebanon is worsening day by day.

This project will support the development of small-to-medium enterprises, working with small business owners and provide guidance and training to enhance resilience and greater livelihood sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
